WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:04.610
 Should I juggle a bit?

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:05.375
 Yeah.

00:00:05.375 --> 00:00:07.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.031
 I've had a long-term
love affair with lemons.

00:00:10.031 --> 00:00:12.486
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:12.486 --> 00:00:13.468
[LAUGHS]

00:00:13.468 --> 00:00:15.930
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:20.960
 This is a world of colors,
intensity, condiments, tahini,

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.380
hummus, muhummara,
everything together.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.510
So it's totally informal, the
opposite of French cooking,

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.440
right?

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.290
See this beautiful smoke?

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.830
That's all flavor.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.010
The one thing I really
don't like is a boring meal.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.950
They want to go,
ah, what was that?

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.790
People think, I can't
cook Middle Eastern.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.250
I don't know how to make my
vegetables taste delicious.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.940
I hope to show you that
you can cook those things,

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.520
and you can do it
really, really well.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.590
Vegetables have an
incredible ability

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.940
to be played with, manipulated
a bit, soak flavors, grilled.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.989
These carrots-- is
very Instagrammable.

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:07.110
This is a very crucial moment.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.110
When you add ice water,
it aerates the hummus,

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.510
makes it even smoother, lighter.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.220
And I'm adding confit garlic.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.280
I can't possibly envisage
a dish without garlic.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.468
That's just not natural.

00:01:20.468 --> 00:01:21.780
[LAUGHS]

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:25.200
Eggplants take on flavors
like nothing else.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.480
There's something
meaty about them.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.520
This dish-- it
happens to be vegan.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.220
I challenge any meat eater
to say it's not perfect.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:37.510
I always like to keep
the last bit for myself.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:39.280
I grew up in the heart
of the Middle East,

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.530
where there's quite a lot
of confrontation going on.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.440
And I found, over the
years, that food is really

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.030
an international language.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:50.120
It has this incredible ability
to bring people together.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.380
I want you to be able to go into
the kitchen without the stress.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.130
I want you to be able
to sit around a table,

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.680
share a meal with your
family and friends,

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.040
and be really proud of
what you've created.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.010
I'm Yotam Ottolenghi, and
this is my MasterClass.

